\ A failed child appears in the deadlock dump with its stored error, linked to
\ the blocked scope body by the shared scope token.
\
\ The child parks on `go` until the cleanup-protected body is running, so the
\ handler is always registered before the failure. The failure cancels the
\ body at its receive, the shielded cleanup handler parks on a channel with no
\ sender, and the scope never exits, so the failed child is never reaped.

use "testing" ;
[
  go: 1 <buffered-channel> ;
  out: <channel> ;
  [ go receive drop 1 0 / ] spawn drop
  [ t go send out receive drop ] [ out receive drop ] cleanup
] task-scope
